claim.claim-text:
a first ultrasonic transducer (201A) for transmitting a first transmitted ultrasonic imaging signal to the object at a first frequency and receiving a first received ultrasonic imaging signal from the object at the first frequency;
an audio transducer for transmitting an audio signal to an object; and
an interference circuit for interfering the first transmitted ultrasonic imaging signal with the audio signal to steer the first transmitted ultrasonic imaging signal to the object.

obtain a first time series of sensor values associated with one or more signals received by the mechanical diaphragm;
obtain a second time series of sensor values associated with one or more signals received by the first ultrasonic transducer;
obtain a third time series of sensor values associated with one or more signals received by the optical sensor;
pass the first time series of sensor values, the second time series of sensor values, and the third time series of sensor values to an autoencoder; and
determine, using the autoencoder, a physiometric parameter associated with the object.

receiving, at a stethoscope head (110) comprising a mechanical diaphragm (200), a stethoscopic audio signal from an object;
transmitting, using an ultrasonic transducer (201A), a transmitted ultrasonic imaging signal to the object at a first frequency;
receiving, using the ultrasonic transducer, a received ultrasonic imaging signal from the object;
transmitting, using an audio transducer, an audio signal to the object; and
interfering, using an interference circuit, the transmitted ultrasonic imaging signal with the audio signal to steer the transmitted ultrasonic imaging signal to the object.
